  "abstract_summary": "Large language models are increasingly composed into agent loops that plan, call tools, and resume the same task after each action. These loops press a shared memory hierarchy harder than conventional multi-turn chat, because they hold a growing key-value (KV) prefix across tool waits and place many sessions on one...",
